new file mode 100644
index 0000000..13196f7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.commit-msg
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Add threshold gating to frai eval
+
+Implement --threshold <metric>=<min> option for frai eval to gate CI on
+metric scores. Allows specifying multiple thresholds, each gating on a
+specific metric's score.
+
+Behavior:
+- Threshold passes when metric.score >= min
+- Metric with no score (score === null) fails its threshold
+- Exit 0 if all thresholds pass or none specified
+- Exit 1 if any threshold fails
+- Exit 2 if malformed threshold or unknown metric
+- Report is written regardless of threshold status
+- JSON reports gain top-level `passed` and `thresholds` array
+- Markdown reports gain "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL status
+
+SDK (frai-core):
+- generateReport() now accepts optional `thresholds` object
+- Works with custom metrics passed to runEvaluations
+- Backward compatible: without thresholds, behavior unchanged
+
+CLI:
+- Add --threshold option to eval command (repeatable)
+- Parse and validate thresholds (format, range, metric ID)
+- List valid metric IDs on unknown metric error
+
+Tests:
+- Add tests for threshold passing, failing, null scores
+- Add test for markdown report with thresholds
+
+Fixes: Allow evaluation to fail CI when metrics don't meet targets
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Haiku 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
